  };
  setCandleData((prevData) => [...prevData.slice(-1)[0].timestamp !== newCandleData.timestamp ? prevData : prevData.slice(0, -1), newCandleData]);
});
```

This will create a WebSocket connection to the Binance API and update the chart with real-time candlestick data. The hook will automatically close the WebSocket connection when the component is unmounted or the `binanceUrl` changes.

Remember that this example may not be fully optimized, but it should give you an idea for using the WebSocket hook in your project.

