There is a bug in the code that causes the first player (Player 0) to always win the most hands.

The issue is related to the way the code handles the determination of the winners. In the `determineWinners` function, the code compares the `tiebreaker` arrays using the `arraysEqual` function. The `arraysEqual` function checks whether two arrays have equal length and equal elements.

However, in some cases, this comparison may not be correct. When players have equal hand ranks, it should not compare the whole arrays, but only the first elements. For example, if two players have two pairs, the code should only compare the first elements of the tiebreakers, not the whole arrays. If the first elements are equal, it should continue to the next elements, and so on.

To fix this bug, you should change the `determineWinners` function to compare the tiebreakers correctly. Here's an updated version of the function:

```javascript
function determineWinners(playerHands, sharedCards) {
    const playerEvaluations = playerHands.map((hand) => evaluateHand(hand.concat(sharedCards)));

    let maxRank = null;
    const winners = [];
    let maxTiebreakers = [];

    for (const { rank, tiebreaker } of playerEvaluations) {
        if (maxRank === null || rank > maxRank) {
            maxRank = rank;
            maxTiebreakers = [tiebreaker];
        } else if (rank === maxRank) {
            maxTiebreakers.push(tiebreaker);
        }
    }

    for (let i = 0; i < playerEvaluations.length; i++) {
        const { rank, tiebreaker } = playerEvaluations[i];

        if (rank !== maxRank) {
            continue;
        }

        if (maxTiebreakers.every((maxTiebreaker) => compareTiebreakers(tiebreaker, maxTiebreaker))) {
            winners.push(i);
        }
    }

    return winners;
}

function compareTiebreakers(a1, a2) {
    for (let i = 0; i < a1.length; i++) {
        if (a1[i] !== a2[i]) {
            return false;
        }
    }
    return true;
}
```

With this change, the results should be more evenly distributed among the players, and you should not see Player 0 winning most of the time anymore.

