To retrieve data from a txt file and add it to a Room database in Android Studio, you can follow these steps:

1. First, create a model class that represents the data you want to add to the database. For example, if your txt file contains a list of books, your model class can be:

```java
@Entity(tableName = "books")
public class Book {
    @PrimaryKey
    @NonNull
    private String id;
    private String title;
    private String author;
    private int year;

    // getters and setters
}
```

2. Then, create a DAO (data access object) interface that defines the methods to interact with the database. For example:

```java
@Dao
public interface BookDao {
    @Query("SELECT * FROM books")
    List<Book> getAll();

    @Insert
    void insertAll(List<Book> books);
}
```

3. Create a Room database that includes your entity (Book) and DAO (BookDao). For example:

```java
@Database(entities = {Book.class}, version = 1, exportSchema = false)
public abstract class AppDatabase extends RoomDatabase {
    public abstract BookDao bookDao();
}
```

4. In your activity or fragment where you want to retrieve the data, create a method to read the txt file and parse its content into a list of Book objects. For example:

```java
private List<Book> readTxtFile() {
    List<Book> books = new ArrayList<>();
    try {
        InputStream inputStream = getAssets().open("books.txt");
        BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(inputStream));
        String line;
        while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
            String[] parts = line.split(",");
            if (parts.length == 4) {
                Book book = new Book();
                book.setId(parts[0]);
                book.setTitle(parts[1]);
                book.setAuthor(parts[2]);
                book.setYear(Integer.parseInt(parts[3]));
                books.add(book);
            }
        }
    } catch (IOException e) {
        e.printStackTrace();
    }
    return books;
}
```

5. Finally, call the DAO's insertAll() method to add the data to the database. For example:

```java
AppDatabase db = Room.databaseBuilder(getApplicationContext(), AppDatabase.class, "my-db").build();
List<Book> books = readTxtFile();
db.bookDao().insertAll(books);
```

Note: Make sure to run the above code in a background thread, as Room database interactions should not be performed on the main thread. You can use an AsyncTask or a separate thread to execute the database operations.

