In this example, we're using the `mutableStateOf` function to create a state variable called `value` that defaults to 0. We then display the value in a `Text` view and provide a button that increments the value. When the button is clicked, we increment the `value` variable and call the `setContent` function again with the same composable function (`MyLayout()`), which triggers the recomposition of the layout.

