In order to recreate DataGrid columns during runtime, you can simply clear the current columns collection and add new columns manually, according to your logic. Here's an example of how you can recreate DataGrid columns in C# and WPF:

First, create a method that clears and recreates the columns:

```csharp
private void RecreateDataGridColumns(DataGrid dataGrid)
{
    // Clear existing columns
    dataGrid.Columns.Clear();

    // Add new columns here
    DataGridTextColumn column1 = new DataGridTextColumn();
    column1.Header = "Column1";
    column1.Binding = new Binding("Property1");
    dataGrid.Columns.Add(column1);

