```

Modify your `MyDataGrid_AutoGeneratingColumn` event to save the original headers:

```csharp
private void MyDataGrid_AutoGeneratingColumn(object sender, DataGridAutoGeneratingColumnEventArgs e)
{
    if (!originalHeaders.ContainsKey(e.Column.Header.ToString()))
    {
        originalHeaders.Add(e.Column.Header.ToString(), e.Column.Header.ToString());
    }

    // Other code that you might have in this event...
}
```

Then, create a method that restores the original column headers:

```csharp
private void RestoreOriginalHeaders(DataGrid dataGrid)
{
    foreach (DataGridColumn column in dataGrid.Columns)
    {
        if (originalHeaders.TryGetValue(column.Header.ToString(), out string originalHeader))
        {
            column.Header = originalHeader;
        }
    }
}
```

Now, you can call this `RestoreOriginalHeaders` method whenever you want to restore the original headers. For example, you can use a button as shown below:

