To calculate shipping rates using the Royal Mail API in JavaScript, you'll need to follow these steps:

1. Sign up for a Royal Mail Developer account if you don't have one already: https://developer.royalmail.net/user/register
2. Sign in to your Developer account, then create an API key from your account's dashboard.
3. Use the API key to make requests to Royal Mail's Shipping API endpoints.

Here's an example of how you can use JavaScript to call the Royal Mail API and calculate shipping rates:

```javascript
// Required modules
const axios = require("axios");

// Your Royal Mail API key
const apiKey = "your_api_key_here";

// Set up axios instance
const royalMailApi = axios.create({
  baseURL: "https://api.royalmail.net/shipping/v3",
  headers: {
    Authorization: `Bearer ${apiKey}`,
  },
});

// Function to get shipping rates
const getShippingRate = async (from, to, weight) => {
  try {
    const response = await royalMailApi.post("/quotes", {
      from: {
        countryCode: from,
      },
      to: {
        countryCode: to,
      },
      weight: weight,
    });

    if (response.data.quotes && response.data.quotes.length > 0) {
      // You can access shipping rate details here:
      const rates = response.data.quotes.map((quote) => {
        return {
          serviceName: quote.service.name,
          deliveryTime: quote.deliveryTime,
          cost: quote.cost.exVat,
        };
      });

      console.log(rates);
    } else {
      console.log("No quotes found");
    }
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error fetching shipping rate:", error.message);
  }
};

// Example usage:
const fromCountryCode = "GB";
const toCountryCode = "US";
const parcelWeight = 1.0; // Weight in kg
getShippingRate(fromCountryCode, toCountryCode, parcelWeight);
```

Replace `your_api_key_here` with your actual API key, and make sure you have Axios installed (`npm install axios`) before running the script. This example uses the axios library to make the HTTP post request to Royal Mail's Shipping API; you can add additional parameters to the request based on Royal Mail's API documentation.

