Next, update the `useEffect` to handle multiple `user_id`s in `referralId`:

```javascript
useEffect(() => {
  referrersList(bearer).then((data) => {
    if (!data) return;
    setReferralList(data.data);
  });

  // Create an array of promises for each user_id in referralId
  const referralPromises = referralId.map((id) =>
    referrerIncomesStatistics(bearer, from, to, id)
  );

  // Wait for all promises to complete and combine the results
  Promise.all(referralPromises).then((results) => {
