Here's a simple PHP script to create a photo album from a folder containing image files. The code assumes all images are in a folder named "images" and checks for '.jpg', '.png', and '.gif' extensions.

To use this code, create a PHP file (e.g., `photo_album.php`) and paste the following code:

```php
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<style>
  .container {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .photo {
    margin: 5px;
    width: calc(33.333% - 10px);
  }

  .photo img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
</style>
<title>Photo Album</title>
</head>
<body>
<h1>My Photo Album</h1>
<div class="container">
<?php
  // Set the images folder name
  $folder_path = 'images/';

  // Set the accepted extensions and initialize the file list
  $extensions_array = ['jpg', 'png', 'gif'];
  $file_list = [];

  // Scan the folder, filter images by extension, and push them into the file list
  if (is_dir($folder_path)) {
    $files = scandir($folder_path);
    foreach ($files as $file) {
      $file_extension = strtolower(pathinfo($file, PATHINFO_EXTENSION));
      if (in_array($file_extension, $extensions_array)) {
        array_push($file_list, $folder_path . $file);
      }
    }
  }

  // Output the image files in the file list
  foreach ($file_list as $image) {
    echo '<div class="photo">';
    echo '<img src="' . $image . '" alt="' . pathinfo($image, PATHINFO_FILENAME) . '">';
    echo '</div>';
  }
?>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

This will create a simple photo gallery displaying images from the "images" folder. Make sure the folder is present in the same directory as the PHP file and contains the necessary images.

