An automated trading solution requires the implementation of several key components to ensure that the trading algorithm operates accurately and effectively. This will involve acquiring real-time data, implementing trading strategies, tracking performance, managing risk, and executing trades through a broker. In this C# solution, we will employ a modular design consisting of multiple classes and interfaces to streamline the development process and make it easier to test and modify individual components.

1. Real-time Data Acquisition

The first step in designing an automated trading solution is acquiring real-time data to feed our algorithm. This is typically accomplished through the use of APIs provided by data providers such as AlphaVantage or a broker's platform.

