#include "SlateBasics.h"
#include "SlateExtras.h"
```

2. Create a Slate button in your widget class by defining an `SButton` shared pointer and a function called `OnButtonClicked` that will be called when the button is clicked:

```cpp
TSharedPtr<SButton> MyButton;
FReply OnButtonClicked();
```

3. Define your `OnButtonClicked` function inside your class:

```cpp
FReply MyWidget::OnButtonClicked()
{
    // Add code to handle the button click event here
    UE_LOG(LogTemp, Warning, TEXT("Button clicked!"));

    return FReply::Handled();
}
```

4. Inside the `Construct` function, create the TSharedPtr for your button and bind the `OnButtonClicked` function to its `OnClicked` event:

```cpp
void MyWidget::Construct(const FArguments& InArgs)
{
    MyButton = SNew(SButton) 
                    .ContentPadding(10) 
                    .VAlign(VAlign_Center) 
                    .HAlign(HAlign_Center) 
                    .Text(FText::FromString("My Button")) 
                    .OnClicked(this, &MyWidget::OnButtonClicked);
}
```

5. Finally, remember to add the button to the widget hierarchy to make it visible. Here's a simple example adding it as a child of a vertical box:

```cpp
void MyWidget::Construct(const FArguments& InArgs)
{
    // ... Create the button as shown in the previous step ...

    // Create a vertical box container
    TSharedPtr<SVerticalBox> Container = SNew(SVerticalBox)
        + SVerticalBox::Slot()
            .AutoSizeHeight()
            .VAlign(VAlign_Center)
            .Padding(10)
            [
                MyButton.ToSharedRef()
            ];

    // Set the widget content 
    ChildSlot
        [
            Container.ToSharedRef()
        ];
}
```

With the above code, you should have a basic Slate button in your UI. You can customize the button appearance, size, and padding by adjusting the values inside the `SNew` call.

Please note that this example assumes you are familiar with creating custom Slate widgets in Unreal Engine. If you are new to Slate, you might want to check the Unreal Engine documentation and some tutorials to get more familiar with the basics of the Slate framework.

