Creating a simple JPEG decoder from scratch without using any external libraries can be quite a complex task, as you would need to handle various aspects of the JPEG standard, such as Huffman coding, quantization tables, and more.

However, it can be a great learning experience if you're interested in delving deeper into JPEG image format and low-level programming. The following code provides a basic outline for a simple C JPEG decoder without using any external libraries. Note that this code is only a starting point, and does not handle all aspects of the JPEG standard. It's highly recommended to use an external library for more robust and efficient handling.

