Add a start script to your `package.json` file that runs your server:

```json
"scripts": {
  "start": "node backend/server.js"
}
```

6. Start the server:

To start the Express.js server, run the following command in your terminal:

```
npm start
```

After running this command, you should see the message "Server is running on port 5000" in the terminal, and your Express.js server is now set up and running.

