2. When the user manually updates the amount field, also update the `isAmountEnteredManually` flag to `true`.

3. Update your side effect logic to only execute when the `isAmountEnteredManually` flag is `false`. If the flag is `true`, the side effect should not update the amount value because the user has already updated it manually.

Here's an updated version of your `amountUpdateHandler` function with this logic:

```javascript
export function* amountUpdateHandler(): Generator<Effect, StepResponse, string> {
  // Check if the amount was entered manually
  const isAmountEnteredManually = yield* select(getAmountEnteredManually);

  if (!isAmountEnteredManually) {
    const totalOfChargesTable = yield* select(paymentTableSelectors.getTotalOfChargesTable);
    const totalOfCreditsTable = yield* select(paymentTableSelectors.getTotalOfCreditsTable);
