3. Create a new EA: In MetaEditor, click on "File" and then "New". Choose "Expert Advisor (template)" and click "Next". Give your EA a name, for example, "SimpleForexRobot", and click "Finish".

4. Initialize the EA: In the newly created MQL4 file, you'll see two predefined functions: `OnInit()` and `OnDeinit()`. These functions are called when the EA is attached/detached or the timeframe/symbol is changed. You can use `OnInit()` to initialize any variables or parameters and `OnDeinit()` to clean up before the EA stops running.

5. Define variables and input parameters: At the beginning of the file, define any variables and input parameters you will use in your EA. For this simple robot, we'll need a few variables:

   ```cpp
   input int StopLoss = 50;
   input int TakeProfit = 100;
   input double LotSize = 0.01;
   input int FastMA = 5;
   input int SlowMA = 20;
   int Ticket = -1;
   double StopLossLevel, TakeProfitLevel;
   int MagicNumber = 12345;
   ```

6. Create a trading function: Create a function called `Trade()` in which you will implement the trading logic of your EA. In this example, we will use a Moving Average Crossover strategy. When the Fast MA crosses above the Slow MA, we'll enter a long trade, and when the Fast MA crosses below the Slow MA, we'll enter a short trade.

   Here's an example of the `Trade()` function:
   ```cpp
   void Trade()
   {
       double FastMAValue = iMA(Symbol(), 0, FastMA, 0, MODE_SMA, PRICE_CLOSE, 1);
       double SlowMAValue = iMA(Symbol(), 0, SlowMA, 0, MODE_SMA, PRICE_CLOSE, 1);
       double PrevFastMAValue = iMA(Symbol(), 0, FastMA, 0, MODE_SMA, PRICE_CLOSE, 2);
       double PrevSlowMAValue = iMA(Symbol(), 0, SlowMA, 0, MODE_SMA, PRICE_CLOSE, 2);

       if (FastMAValue > SlowMAValue && PrevFastMAValue <= PrevSlowMAValue) // Long trade
       {
           if (Ticket != -1) // Close existing short position, if any
           {
               OrderClose(Ticket, LotSize, Bid, 3);
           }
           Ticket = OrderSend(Symbol(), OP_BUY, LotSize, Ask, 3, StopLossLevel, TakeProfitLevel, "Long Trade", MagicNumber, 0, clrBlue);
       }
       else if (FastMAValue < SlowMAValue && PrevFastMAValue >= PrevSlowMAValue) // Short trade
       {
           if (Ticket != -1) // Close existing long position, if any
           {
               OrderClose(Ticket, LotSize, Ask, 3);
           }
           Ticket = OrderSend(Symbol(), OP_SELL, LotSize, Bid, 3, StopLossLevel, TakeProfitLevel, "Short Trade", MagicNumber, 0, clrRed);
       }
   }
   ```

7. Adding the `Trade()` function to `OnTick()`: The `OnTick()` function will execute every time there's a new quote movement in the market. Place the `Trade()` function inside the `OnTick()` function.

   ```cpp
   void OnTick()
   {
       StopLossLevel = Ask - StopLoss * Point;
       TakeProfitLevel = Ask + TakeProfit * Point;
       Trade();
   }    
   ```

8. Compile the EA: Save your EA and click the "Compile" button in MetaEditor. Ensure there are no errors in the "Errors" tab.

9. Test the EA: In MT4, open the Strategy Tester by clicking on "View" and then "Strategy Tester" or pressing Ctrl+R. Choose your EA, the currency pair, and the timeframe. Set the test period and click "Start" to test your EA.

