2. Create a new Java class called `WebsiteImageRipper.java`. This class will contain the main method and logic for downloading images from a given URL.

```java
import org.jsoup.Jsoup;
import org.jsoup.nodes.Document;
import org.jsoup.nodes.Element;
import org.jsoup.select.Elements;

import java.io.BufferedInputStream;
import java.io.FileOutputStream;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.io.InputStream;
import java.net.URL;

public class WebsiteImageRipper {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Make sure there is a URL argument
        if (args.length != 1) {
            System.out.println("Usage: java WebsiteImageRipper <URL>");
            return;
        }

        try {
            // Fetch the HTML content from the specified URL
            Document document = Jsoup.connect(args[0]).get();
            // Select all the image elements
            Elements images = document.select("img[src~=(?i)\\.(png|jpe?g|gif)]");

            System.out.println("Found " + images.size() + " images");

            // Download each image
            int i = 0;
            for (Element img : images) {
                String imgUrl = img.absUrl("src");
                System.out.println("Downloading image " + (i + 1) + ": " + imgUrl);
                downloadImage(imgUrl, "img" + i + ".jpg");
                i++;
            }

            System.out.println("Finished downloading images");
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
            System.err.println("Error processing the URL: " + args[0]);
        }
    }

    private static void downloadImage(String imageUrl, String destinationFile) throws IOException {
        try (InputStream in = new BufferedInputStream(new URL(imageUrl).openStream());
             FileOutputStream fileOutputStream = new FileOutputStream(destinationFile)) {
            byte dataBuffer[] = new byte[1024];
            int bytesRead;
            while ((bytesRead = in.read(dataBuffer, 0, 1024)) != -1) {
                fileOutputStream.write(dataBuffer, 0, bytesRead);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

3. Compile and run the Java program by executing the following command in your terminal:

```sh
javac WebsiteImageRipper.java
java WebsiteImageRipper https://example.com
```

Replace `https://example.com` with the URL that contains your posts' images. The images will be downloaded to the same directory where the Java program is executed.

Keep in mind that you might need to adjust the image selector (the `img[src~=(?i)\\.(png|jpe?g|gif)]` part) according to the website's structure. In case you want to download images only from your own posts, you should use a more specific selector based on the HTML structure of the website.

