To resolve the compiler error, you can use a combination of `std::ostringstream` to build the formatted string and then print it using `printf` or other logging methods. Here's the modified `IMF_LOG` function that does this:

```cpp
#include <sstream>
#include <cstdio>
#include <string>
#include <SDL2/SDL.h>

template<typename T>
void append_format(std::ostringstream& stream, T arg) {
    stream << arg;
}

template<typename T, typename... Args>
void append_format(std::ostringstream& stream, T arg, Args... args) {
    stream << arg;
    append_format(stream, args...);
}

template <typename... Args>
void IMF_LOG(std::string format, Args const&... args)
{
    std::ostringstream stream;
    append_format(stream, format.c_str(), "\n", args...);
    std::string result = stream.str();

    SDL_LockMutex(m_loggerMutex);
    printf("%s", result.c_str());
    SDL_UnlockMutex(m_loggerMutex);
}
```

The `append_format` function is added to handle appending the format string and arguments to the `std::ostringstream`. This function is called in the `IMF_LOG` function, where it appends the appropriate strings and arguments to the stream. After that, we use `printf` to print the resulting formatted string.

