You can check if a button is enabled in WPF C# by accessing the `IsEnabled` property of the button. Here is an example to check if the button is enabled when the application is launched for the first time:

1. First, add a name to the button in the XAML code:

```xml
<Button x:Name="myButton" Content="Click Me" IsEnabled="True" />
```

2. In the code-behind file, you can check the `IsEnabled` property of the button in the `Window_Loaded` event handler:

```csharp
private void Window_Loaded(object sender, RoutedEventArgs e)
{
    if (myButton.IsEnabled)
    {
        MessageBox.Show("Button is enabled on first launch.");
    }
}
```

If the button is enabled, the message box will be displayed. If it is disabled, nothing will happen.

