To create a minimal JS+PHP webpage analytics system to track the necessary data of the user, we can use the following steps:

Step 1: Create a PHP file to receive the data and save it into a .log file (log.php)

```php
<?php
if (!empty($_POST['data'])) {
    $data = $_POST['data'];
    $log_file = fopen('analytics.log', 'a');
    fwrite($log_file, $data . PHP_EOL);
    fclose($log_file);
}
?>
```

Step 2: Create the JavaScript (analytics.js) to collect and send the data to the PHP file:

```javascript
function gatherData() {
  const data = {
    ip: '', // To be filled in by PHP
    referrer: document.referrer,
    location: {}, // To be filled in by an IP geolocation API
    browserInfo: navigator.userAgent,
    device: '', // To be filled in by a library to detect device properties
    url: window.location.href,
    title: document.title,
    userBehavior: {}, // To be filled in with event listeners for clicks, scrolls etc.
    preferences: navigator.language || navigator.userLanguage,
    demographics: {}, // To be filled in, potentially by a user login system
  };

  return data;
}

function sendData(data) {
  fetch('/log.php', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({ data: JSON.stringify(data) }),
  });
}

async function getUserIP() {
  const response = await fetch('https://api.ipify.org?format=json');
  const ipData = await response.json();
  return ipData.ip;
}

async function getLocationData(ip) {
  // Replace {API_KEY} with your actual key.
  const response = await fetch(`http://ip-api.com/json/${ip}?fields=status,country,regionName,city,zip,lat,lon`);
  const locationData = await response.json();
  return locationData;
}

(async () => {
  const data = gatherData();
  data.ip = await getUserIP();
  data.location = await getLocationData(data.ip);
  sendData(data);
})();
```

