Step 5: Create a custom authentication success handler
Step 6: Implement a user details service
Step 7: Test your implementation

Now, let's discuss each step in detail.

Step 1: Set up your Spring Boot project
To get started, create a new Spring Boot project using either Spring Initializr (https://start.spring.io/) or your favorite IDE. Generate the project with the default options selected.

Step 2: Add required dependencies
Add the following dependencies to your `pom.xml` (Maven) or `build.gradle` (Gradle):
- Spring Security: Required for the security configuration.
- Spring Security OAuth2 Client: Required for OAuth2 client features.
- Spring Security OAuth2 JOSE: Required for JWT support.

For Maven, add these dependencies:

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-security</artifactId>
</dependency>
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-security-oauth2-client</artifactId>
</dependency>
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
