  );
}

export default App;
```

In this example, we are using the `useState` and `useEffect` hooks to manage the state of the data and loading indicators. The `useEffect` hook is used to fetch the data from the backend API using Axios. Once the data is fetched, it is stored in the `data` state and the `loading` state is set to `false`.

In the return statement, we are conditionally rendering a loading message or the data itself depending on the value of the `loading` state. If `loading` is `true`, we display a loading message. Otherwise, we iterate over the `data` array and render each item as a list item.

