Here we are initializing Sequelize with our database credentials and storing the sequelize instance in an object called db, which we will use to import the sequelize instance throughout our application.

3. Creating a Model

Create a new file in the models folder called ExampleModel.js and add the following code:

```javascript
const sequelize = require('./index.js').sequelize;
const Sequelize = require('./index.js').Sequelize;

const ExampleModel = sequelize.define('example_model', {
  column1: {
    type: Sequelize.STRING,
  },
  column2: {
    type: Sequelize.INTEGER,
  },
  column3: {
    type: Sequelize.DATE,
  },
}, {
  timestamps: false,
});

module.exports = ExampleModel;
```

Here we are defining a new model with 3 columns. We are also disabling timestamps which are not always necessary.

4. Creating a Controller

Create a new folder in the root of your project called controllers. This folder will contain all of your application's controllers.

Create a new file in the controllers folder called ExampleController.js and add the following code:

```javascript
const ExampleModel = require('../models/ExampleModel');

module.exports = {
  async create(req, res) {
    try {
      const instance = await ExampleModel.create(req.body);
      return res.status(201).json(instance);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error(error);
      return res.status(500).json(error);
    }
  },
};
```

Here we are defining a new controller with a create method. This method will receive data from request body, create a new model instance then respond with the newly created data.

5. Creating a Route

Create a new file in the root of your project called routes.js and add the following code:

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const ExampleController = require('./controllers/ExampleController');

const router = express.Router();

router.post('/examples', ExampleController.create);

module.exports = router;
```

Here we are creating a new route to handle POST requests to '/examples'. This route will call the create method defined in ExampleController.

6. Configuring Express

Open the server.js file and add the following code:

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const bodyParser = require('body-parser');
