To send a message and receive a BasicNack in C# using the RabbitMQ.Client library, follow these steps:

1. Install the RabbitMQ.Client NuGet package to your project.

2. Import the necessary namespaces:

```csharp
using System.Text;
using RabbitMQ.Client;
using RabbitMQ.Client.Events;
```

3. Create a connection and a model (channel) to communicate with RabbitMQ:

```csharp
ConnectionFactory factory = new ConnectionFactory() { HostName = "localhost" };
using IConnection connection = factory.CreateConnection();
using IModel channel = connection.CreateModel();
```

4. Enable publisher confirms for the channel:

```csharp
channel.ConfirmSelect();
```

5. Declare the exchange and queue:

```csharp
channel.ExchangeDeclare("exchange_name", "direct");
channel.QueueDeclare("queue_name", durable: true, exclusive: false, autoDelete: false);
channel.QueueBind("queue_name", "exchange_name", "routing_key");
```

6. Handle the BasicNack and BasicAck events:

```csharp
channel.BasicNacks += (sender, args) =>
{
    Console.WriteLine($"Message Nacked, deliveryTag: {args.DeliveryTag}, multiple: {args.Multiple}");
};

channel.BasicAcks += (sender, args) =>
{
    Console.WriteLine($"Message Acked, deliveryTag: {args.DeliveryTag}, multiple: {args.Multiple}");
};
```

7. Send a message:

```csharp
IBasicProperties properties = channel.CreateBasicProperties();
properties.Persistent = true;

byte[] body = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes("Hello, nack this message!");

channel.BasicPublish("exchange_name", "routing_key", mandatory: false, properties, body: body);
```

8. Set up a consumer to consume and reject (BasicNack) the message:

```csharp
var consumer = new EventingBasicConsumer(channel);

consumer.Received += (model, ea) =>
{
    var body = ea.Body.ToArray();
    var message = Encoding.UTF8.GetString(body);

    Console.WriteLine("Message received: {0}", message);

    // Reject the message with BasicNack (requeue: false, multiple: false)
    channel.BasicNack(ea.DeliveryTag, multiple: false, requeue: false);
};

channel.BasicConsume(queue: "queue_name", autoAck: false, consumer: consumer);
```

9. Finally, if you want to wait for publisher confirms (BasicAck):

```csharp
channel.WaitForConfirmsOrDie(new TimeSpan(0, 0, 5)); // 5 seconds timeout
```

Now, when you run this code, it will send a message and receive a BasicNack from the consumer.

