To perform these operations using Java Spark, first create two datasets, then use the `union()` function to combine them, followed by the `groupByKey()` function to group them by ID, and finally apply the `mapValues()` function to process the group values. Here's an example:

```java
import org.apache.spark.api.java.JavaPairRDD;
import org.apache.spark.api.java.JavaRDD;
import org.apache.spark.api.java.JavaSparkContext;
import org.apache.spark.SparkConf;
import scala.Tuple2;

import java.util.Arrays;

public class SparkUnionExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SparkConf sparkConf = new SparkConf().setMaster("local").setAppName("SparkUnionExample");
        JavaSparkContext sc = new JavaSparkContext(sparkConf);

        // Create two datasets
        JavaRDD<String> input1 = sc.parallelize(Arrays.asList("1,Alice", "2,Bob", "3,Charlie"));
        JavaRDD<String> input2 = sc.parallelize(Arrays.asList("3,Daniel", "4,Eva", "5,Frank"));

        // Convert the datasets into JavaPairRDDs
        JavaPairRDD<Integer, String> dataset1 = input1.mapToPair(line -> {
            String[] parts = line.split(",");
            Integer id = Integer.parseInt(parts[0]);
            String name = parts[1];
            return new Tuple2<>(id, name);
        });

        JavaPairRDD<Integer, String> dataset2 = input2.mapToPair(line -> {
            String[] parts = line.split(",");
            Integer id = Integer.parseInt(parts[0]);
            String name = parts[1];
            return new Tuple2<>(id, name);
        });

        // Union the datasets
        JavaPairRDD<Integer, String> unionDataset = dataset1.union(dataset2);

        // Group by ID
        JavaPairRDD<Integer, Iterable<String>> groupedDataset = unionDataset.groupByKey();

        // Call a map function on the values
        JavaPairRDD<Integer, Integer> result = groupedDataset.mapValues(names -> {
            int count = 0;
            for (String name : names) {
                count++;
            }
            return count;
        });

        System.out.println("Result: " + result.collect());
        }
}
```

This example demonstrates how to create two datasets, union them, and then apply a map function after grouping by ID. The output will be a list of tuples containing the ID and the count of the names after grouping.

