This function takes an array of objects (e.g., your `data`) and transforms it into the desired format. In the transformed data, for each original object, there is now an array containing objects in the form `{prop:'item[index]', text:'any value'}`. The `prop` key will show the original key as "item.key" and the `text` key will contain the original value.

The `transformData` function uses two nested loops to iterate through your data. The first loop iterates over each object in the data array, and the second loop iterates over each key-value pair in the current object. It then adds a new transformed object to `transformedItem` and, after transforming everything from the current object, pushes the `transformedItem` into the `transformedData` array.

