It seems that there is still an unresolved reference issue related to `AppCompatActivity`. This issue can be caused by a missing dependency or the incorrect AndroidX version being used. First, please make sure you have implemented the required dependencies for AppCompat in your `app/build.gradle` file:

```gradle
dependencies {
    // ...
    implementation 'androidx.appcompat:appcompat:<version>'
    // ...
}
```

Replace `<version>` with the latest or your preferred version. It should automatically update the version to the latest compatible version to match your compileSdk/API level. A recommended version is `1.3.1` at the time of writing.

As for why we are using `AppCompatActivity`: the `AppCompatActivity` class is a subclass of `androidx.activity.ComponentActivity` that adds support for action bars, which are used in traditional Android app design. It replaces the older `ActionBarActivity` and is part of the AndroidX library, allowing you to access modern UI components and follow newer UI design guidelines.

When you initially created the app, it might have created an `Activity` that extends `ComponentActivity` directly or another compatible type, like `android.app.Activity`. Using `AppCompatActivity` ensures you can use the necessary UI components and follow current design guidelines, even for older Android versions.

In summary, add the missing `appcompat` dependency and make sure you have the correct AndroidX dependencies in your `app/build.gradle` file. The unresolved reference error should be resolved, allowing you to continue building your application.

