I have written a program that simulates the first round of EuroLeague. This program reads team names and match results from a text file and updates their scores accordingly.

Create a text file in the same directory as your source code and name it "matches.txt". The file should have the following structure:

```
Team1 Team2 Team3 Team4
Team1 Team2 90 85
Team3 Team4 75 80
```

Here is the C program to read the data from "matches.txt" and calculate the first round results:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

#define MAX_TEAMS 32
#define MAX_TEAM_NAME_LEN 20
#define MAX_FILENAME_LEN 100

typedef struct {
    char name[MAX_TEAM_NAME_LEN];
    int points_for;
    int points_against;
} Team;

void update_team(Team *team, int points_for, int points_against) {
    team->points_for += points_for;
    team->points_against += points_against;
}

int main() {
    FILE *file;
    Team teams[MAX_TEAMS];
    int team_count = 0;
    char filename[MAX_FILENAME_LEN] = "matches.txt";

    file = fopen(filename, "r");
    if (file == NULL) {
        printf("Error opening file.\n");
        return 1;
    }

    // Read team names
    while (fscanf(file, "%s", teams[team_count].name) != EOF) {
        teams[team_count].points_for = 0;
        teams[team_count].points_against = 0;
        team_count++;
    }

    // Process matches
    int points1, points2;
    char team_name1[MAX_TEAM_NAME_LEN], team_name2[MAX_TEAM_NAME_LEN];
    fseek(file, 0, SEEK_SET);
    while (fscanf(file, "%s %s %d %d", team_name1, team_name2, &points1, &points2) != EOF) {
        for (int i = 0; i < team_count; i++) {
            if (strcmp(teams[i].name, team_name1) == 0) {
                update_team(&teams[i], points1, points2);
            } else if (strcmp(teams[i].name, team_name2) == 0) {
                update_team(&teams[i], points2, points1);
            }
        }
    }

    fclose(file);

    // Print team results
    printf("\nResults after first round:\n");
    for (int team_id = 0; team_id < team_count; team_id++) {
        printf("Team: %s - Points For: %d - Points Against: %d\n",
            teams[team_id].name,
            teams[team_id].points_for,
            teams[team_id].points_against);
    }

    return 0;
}
```

To compile and run this program:

1. Save the code in a file called "euroleague.c".
2. Open a terminal/command prompt.
3. Navigate to the folder containing the source file and the "matches.txt" file.
4. Compile the program using GCC by entering `gcc -o euroleague euroleague.c`.
5. Execute the compiled program by entering `./euroleague` (Linux or macOS) or `euroleague` (Windows).

